@startuml
title Pipeline fine-tuning - Activation conditionnelle C6 et C7
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false

actor "Expert metier" as Expert

package "Donnees d'apprentissage" {
  [PDF ConOps / OpsCon annotes] as Docs
  [Gold standards JSON] as Gold
  [expert_validation.csv] as ExpertCSV
}
package "Construction dataset" {
  [dataset_builder.py] as DatasetBuilder
  [QualityFilter\nconditionnel] as QualityFilter
  [Split train / validation] as Split
  [train_dataset.jsonl] as TrainJSONL
  [validation_dataset.jsonl] as ValidationJSONL
}
package "Entrainement LoRA" {
  [train_lora.py] as Trainer
  [Base model\nMistral / Llama / Qwen] as BaseModel
  [LoRA adapter\nmodels/conops-lora] as Lora
}
package "Registre modeles" {
  [model_registry.json\nconditionnel] as Registry
  [fine_tuned_provider.py\nreadiness checks] as FineTunedProvider
}
package "Evaluation apres entrainement" {
  [experiment_runner.py] as Runner
  [C6 = fine-tuned model] as C6
  [C7 = fine-tuned model + RAG] as C7
  [precision, recall, F1,\ngrounding, stabilite] as Metrics
}

Expert --> ExpertCSV : validation / correction
Docs --> DatasetBuilder
Gold --> DatasetBuilder
ExpertCSV --> DatasetBuilder
DatasetBuilder --> QualityFilter
QualityFilter --> Split
Split --> TrainJSONL
Split --> ValidationJSONL
TrainJSONL --> Trainer
ValidationJSONL --> Trainer : eval_dataset
BaseModel --> Trainer
Trainer --> Lora
Lora --> Registry
Registry --> FineTunedProvider
FineTunedProvider --> Runner
Runner --> C6
Runner --> C7
C6 --> Metrics
C7 --> Metrics
ValidationJSONL --> Metrics : evaluation hors entrainement

note right of Trainer
Le pipeline s'active avec un adaptateur valide.
Un entrainement exploitable exige un dataset
suffisant, annote et valide par expert.
Le split train/validation limite le risque
de mesurer uniquement la memorisation.
end note

note bottom
C6 : modele fine-tune sans RAG.
C7 : modele fine-tune avec RAG.
Comparaison avec C1, C3, C4 et C5.
end note
@enduml
